-- title:
--   Unramifiedness away from j=0,1728 and the cusps, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for the group $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ attached to $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction of units $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$. Let $K_0$ be the corresponding base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, and assume $K_0 \le K$. Let $j \in K$ have underlying Laurent series the image under `coeffEmb L` of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the series $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series `jNumQ`. Let $P$ be a place of $K$ over $L$, i.e. a valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $L$, distinct from $K$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and suppose $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) = 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_P(j-1728) = 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_P$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation. Then the ramification index of $P$ along the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$ — the infimum of the positive naturals of the form $\operatorname{ord}_P(f)$ for nonzero $f \in K_0$ — equals $1$.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ case of the assertion that the covering $X_H(q^2M') \to X_0(M')$, for $H$ the kernel of reduction of units modulo $q$, is unramified at every place which is neither a cusp nor lies above $j \in \{0,1728\}$; the two order hypotheses encode precisely that $j$ and $j-1728$ are units at $P$. It feeds the unramifiedness statements at height-one places used on the semistable covering analysis for $q=2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_eq_one_of_ord_eq_zero_of_ord_sub_eq_zero_xH_levelH_of_eq_two.lean

